@author "Claude (Anthropic)"

; Element order is semantic. The convention-ordered incenter rabbit ear,
; (--ea .a)(--ec .c) leading, whose arc below a half-turn is the big stayer
; sector, folds cleanly (flatten-rabbit-ear-toward-a.bel). Reorder the same
; three creases so that the leading pair is (--eb .b)(--ea .a): the arc is
; now a small folding sector, and the ear is anchored on material that has
; to move. Every state reaches past the sheet, so the outline ranks none
; above another (spec multifold, "The outline ranks the states of every fan"),
; and both segments of --ea fold. Reordering the items, and nothing else,
; turns a fold into an error.

paper square

mark (through .a .c) as --diag
mark (map --ab onto --diag) as --ea
mark (map --ab onto --bc) as --eb
mark (map --bc onto --diag) as --ec

flatten (--eb & .b) (--ea) (--ec) (emergent beside .a)

; expect error "--ea is ambiguous at the vertex"
